Hello,

I need to vdump a filesystem on one box to a magentic tape on the
other.  I would use rdump on the systems, but that is not supported
under ADVFS, so I must use vdump.  There does not seem to be a rvdump or
vrdump that would perform the same type features a rdump would.

I have tried the following:

mt -f /dev/rmt0h rewind
rsh my_remote_server "/sbin/vdump -0uf - /" | dd of=/dev/nrmt0h

but when I try to do "/sbin/vrestore -if /dev/rmt0h" (after rewinding
the tape), I get:

vrestore: Date of the vdump save-set: Thu Jan 30 16:11:47 1997
vrestore: unable to read from device '/dev/rmt0h'; incomplete read 512 <
33580
DECthreads Last Chance handler: thread 1 exiting on status exception
0x177db005
Exception: Invalid memory address (dce / thd)
Resources lost(coredump)

Does anyone know why this happens and or how to fix it and or a
different way to do this?  I really would rather not nfsmount the
filesystems from the other system.

Thanks,

Rich
rdschramm@scripps.com



