Richard Barndt (richard@imt.net) wrote:
: We have an in-house server product which helps us manage remote recompile
: and distribution issues across all our supported platforms.  The main
: process receives recompile and copy commands and relays them to the rest of
: the platforms, allowing us to recompile on 7 machines with a single
: command.  

Put an entry into /etc/inittab (using chinit) to have root "su" to 
the account name and execute the needed commands.  Putting startup
commands into the inittab file makes upgrading (or applying PTFs)
simpler, since you don't have to worry about any AIX system files
being overwritten in the process.

