I am also a  Oracle DBA. i use advfs and i like it.
I have no bad experiences with it.
I use only the command interface because it is simple and handy.
i do not use the extra advfs utilities. For Oracle i use only one disk
per file domain, and some filesets per domain with only a few data
files per fileset. So i can use vdump -Z and vrestore the move around
the filessets. 
If you use some disks per domain oracle must recover all disks in this
domain if one crashes, wich costs time to recover.
You can use LSM to mirror the disks to get a very high uptime even in
case of a disk failiure, so Oracle will not know about your failiure.

