> Can anyone suggest what's wrong and how to resolve it?  Thanks.

I just encountered the same problem.  I could get the IDL compiler to
execute by setting the _RLD_ARGS environment variable to
"-ignore_unresolved".
However, the next problem you should encounter occurs when you try to
run
your server.  The Orbix libraries appear to be dependent on symbols
in the pthread library that are not present on Digital Unix 4.0.
No amount of fiddling with the run-time loader settings would let me
get the server running, and I don't think I'd trust the server to
operate
correctly even if I could get it running.

At this point, I've concluded that Orbix2.0MT is not compatible with DU
4.0.
I'm waiting to hear from Iona about when DU 4.0 will be supported.

Mark Spruiell
Lawrence Livermore National Lab
mes@llnl.gov



