10.10 releases of HP-UX that 90+ percent of the CPU is consumed by the
process.  I am finding that under 10.20 on a K-410 that it consumes
approximately 33% of the CPU when you are actually doing work with the
tool.  This is a dramatic improvement over the previous versions of the
operating system, in that it seems that the 90+% utilization occurs
whether you are actually doing something or not.  I have also looked at
