Jeff,

Your assumptions are correct - the old bindings will be there, and will
still be served
by CDS (CDS is not a monitor and won't ever remove the entries).  

However, your client code should be smart enough to handle this by looping
through the partial bindings that are returned until an entry is found that
will actually respond, so stale bindings are typically not a big deal. 
Most servers (including yours from the description of the behavior) are
written to register themselves with CDS, so if you don't like the fact that
the old entries are there, you can usually blow away the server
registration in CDS (rpcentry delete), restart the server and it will
recreate a clean/valid entry for itself.

Hope this helps,
Mike Wierzbinski

