Hi

We are running various Alpha's, with DU3.2C, 3.2D, 4.0 and 4.0A, We installed 
Patrol on some of our servers at the beginning of the year ( system monitoring 
s/w ) and noticed that the amount of memory being used by our apps wasn't 
anywhere near that actual RAM in the machines, which was leading to hugh 
amounts of paging and poor performance. 


We tuned some of them to reduce the value of ucb-maximum ( maximum % of memory 
that the ucb's can grow to, which by default is 100%, which is fine for an NFS 
file server, but definitly not a good thing on our DB front-end ), which 
reduced some of our problems. We have changed our swapping from immediate to 
lazy on one of our machines ( running squid web cache ), which also helped the 
amount of paging.


Now we are still trying to tune the web cache, as the number of wired pages 
from vmstat is still high ( 25% ) of memory, and we never get it back when 
squid is killed. What is wired memory  and how can we see what processes are 
causing it to grow, so we can do something about them.

Thanx

Brenden




