Bonnie & iozone are common.  Bonnie tests the speed of file I/O using
standard C library calls.  It does reads and writes of blocks, per
character read and write tests & seek tests.

I seem to remember running bonnie under Digital UNIX 3.2C sometime
last year, so I'm fairly certain you should be able to make it work.
You can get Bonnie at ftp://ftp.sunet.se/pub/benchmark/Bonnie/Bonnie.tar.Z

I've not played much w/iozone, I think you can get it at
ftp://ftp.cs.uni-sb.de/pub/others/iozone-2.01.shar.gz

Cheers,

Drew



